WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.770
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.770
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.770
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:44.450
Chapter 9

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:44.450
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.450
Reinhard's life
is basically simple.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:11.110
Perhaps because he was born to the <i>Reichsritter</i> class, an aristocrat in name only and not very well-to-do...

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:15.890
...he leads a life unlike a Rear Admiral, more like that of an Ensign or other low-ranking officer.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:21.470
It's not that he is truly stingy - it's more
like he is used to thrift than anything else.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:27.210
On this day, too, he was invited to
a party at the Grimmelshausen's...

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:32.890
...but he was walking there alone, without the
accompaniment of a chauffeur or a retainer.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.670
Oh, Baroness Westpfahl.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.100
Long time no see.
Where are you headed ?

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:52.140
I'm invited to a party for Viscount Grimmelshausen in celebration of his recent promotion to Admiral.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:52.920
I see.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.320
What a shame.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.130
If you weren't busy, I would have
taken you to a concert or something.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.460
I'm sorry to
miss your invitation.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.070
You're alone today ?

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.770
This is quite rare.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:09.570
If you're talking about Kircheis, he's attending
a strategy meeting for sub-commanders.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.380
Say hello to
him for me, too.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.640
Tell him that he's
welcome at my salons.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.770
Of course, I will be sure to tell him.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:22.770
Okay then.
I'll see you later.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:31.790
Baroness Magdalena Westpfahl is one of the
few women Reinhard feels heavily indebted to.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:36.320
She is a Baroness by
birth and not by marriage.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.770
As she is both beautiful and intelligent
and also spiritually mature...

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:47.620
...she would've been a major figure in
politics if she had been born a man.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.800
But there is another reason
for which Reinhard respects her.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.510
Reinhard's sister, Annerose,
is isolated in the aristocratic social circles.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:00.410
It was only natural that, because
she was born of a poor <i>Reichsritter...</i>

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:04.250
...she was disliked by the aristocrats
who value lineage and family ranks.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.550
Even ones who didn't actively dislike her
wouldn't have anything to do with her...

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:15.700
...for fear that they, too, might earn the
aristocrats' hostility by befriending her.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:22.970
But Magdalena courageously,
or nonchalantly, befriended Annerose...

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.630
...with no regards to lineage
or other aristocrats' antagonism.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:33.550
One aristocrat criticized her, saying
"How dare a woman try to break tradition !"

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:37.870
You're a man and have no talent
other than to criticize a woman ?

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:43.380
But he was counter-attacked and
couldn't attend social functions for a while.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.120
Oh, my...

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.100
You're Miss Hilda
from Count Mariendorf's.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.650
It's been a long time,
Baroness Westpfahl.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.880
You're still going
to school, aren't you ?

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.730
Yes, I'm graduating next year.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.680
And you'll be going
to college afterwards ?

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.780
Yes !

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.120
The late Countess Mariendorf...

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:13.450
...used to teach classical music at a
school sponsored by the Westpfahls.

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:17.650
But her daughter Hildegard, a.k.a. Hilda...

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.870
...seemed to be more interested in
political and military sciences than arts.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.970
Hilda, if you were a man, you'd be getting
a post in the Ministry of Home Affairs.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.500
Or would you prefer to be an admiral
at the Ministry of Military Affairs ?

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:38.920
Lady Westpfahl would look good
in the uniform of a Fleet Admiral.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.860
In that case, I'd be willing to serve as one
of the general staff under your command.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.300
That's not such a bad idea.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.420
How about I give you a lift ?

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.580
I'll take you
anywhere you want.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.790
I'd like to take up on your offer.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:02.620
By the way, Hilda, haven't
you found a boyfriend yet ?

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:03.300
No.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.830
Would you be willing to
introduce me to someone ?

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.320
Let's see.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.920
I might have someone in mind.

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:11.870
You wouldn't like a man
with no brains, I guess.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:18.980
It sometimes takes so much time for
two people to cover so little distance.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:23.730
It took about another 1000 days
before Reinhard and Hilda met.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:29.000
That was because Baroness Westpfahl
herself was busy with her own love affairs...

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:34.940
...and her role as a patron of arts that she
didn't have time for other people's romances.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:46.830
The party at the Viscount
Grimmelshausen's was quite a joyous affair.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:50.220
It wasn't so much because
of the host's popularity;

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.320
In this nation where
there's no Congress...

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:57.790
...decisions or proposals on political and national issues were often made during these kinds of parties.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:04.370
For that reason, parties are important, can't-miss events for high-ranking officials in the military and politics.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:07.670
That tendency was seen
in this party, too...

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:13.220
...and many discussions were mixed
with alcohol and held in private rooms.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:17.670
Reinhard had nothing
to do with such cliques...

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.900
...and since he had no one in
particular to converse with...

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:25.770
...he busied himself
satisfying his youthful appetite.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:30.080
I want to take some of this
food home for Kircheis.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.580
There was no way Reinhard
could have known this...

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:47.140
...but Luneberg was called to a private room
by his brother-in-law, Count Hartenburg.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:51.460
Count Hartenburg was
then 48 years of age.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:55.590
He was presently employed as a
Sub-Commissioner of the Police Force...

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:58.660
...and was the most likely candidate
to become the next Commissioner.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:04.230
It was rumored that he'd then be promoted
to be the Secretary of the Interior.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.780
He was the brother of
Luneberg's wife, Elizabeth...

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:11.180
...and was probably the only person
in the Empire that Luneberg feared.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.940
Count...

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:22.180
Rear Admiral Luneberg, I've heard some
disturbing stories about your household.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:27.520
Did Elizabeth say
something to you ?

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.750
My sister hasn't said a word.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:38.860
I wish she would express herself
more and keep to herself less.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:46.670
But even though she didn't say
anything, it's gotten around.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:51.600
And your attitude toward her
hasn't exactly been perfect, either.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:59.600
Especially now that a strange rumor is
circulating, I'd like you to behave yourself.

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:06.870
Rear Admiral, I don't like to think
that you married my sister...

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:10.430
...only to gain the political
influence the Hartenburg family has.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:16.500
That would mean I made a mistake
when I promoted your marriage to her.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:22.510
But I can't exchange my pride
for my sister's happiness.

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:30.150
If the marriage is unsalvageable,
appropriate action must be taken.

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:34.860
There's one thing
I'd like to ask, Count.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:35.870
What is it ?

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:38.590
It's about Elizabeth's former fiancé.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:43.890
When you proposed to Elizabeth, I thought
you said you had no interest in her past.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:49.100
Does that mean
you were lying to her ?

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:55.100
Lies are permissible actions
within the Free Planets Alliance, but...

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.570
I appreciate your
sense of irony, Count...

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:02.820
...but the one who is obsessed
with the past is Elizabeth, not me.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:08.550
She always looks for the shadow of her
former fiancé regardless of my presence.

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:12.630
She denies it,
but I know it's true.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:19.670
I see, she's obsessed with the past
and you're worried about the present.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:24.670
I see the Lunebergs have
their individual concerns...

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:28.230
...but which one of you plans
to look after the "future" ?

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.540
At least, I do.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.610
That's all very well.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:43.750
Rear Admiral, don't you dare
disappoint me any further.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.650
I'm sorry.

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:32.200
It seems I mistook
this for an exit.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:40.470
Is anything wrong
with you, Frau ?

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.770
My chest hurts...

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.720
I'll call for
help immediately.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:53.830
I think it's better
if you lie down...

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:02.770
Rear Admiral Musel is interested
in someone else's wife ?

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.440
Darling, why are you
misunderstanding this ?

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:14.820
Lord Musel had me lie
down here because I was ill.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:18.570
You shouldn't say
something so rude...

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:22.200
Rear Admiral Musel, I'd
like to hear your excuse.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.790
"Excuse" ?

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:28.280
Why should I owe
you an "excuse" ?

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.930
The circumstances are as
your lady explains them.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:34.770
I don't plan on
asking for gratitude...

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.770
...but I'm profoundly offended by
your treatment of this situation.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.770
I'm sure you're "offended..."

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:44.050
...since you met someone you truly didn't
want to meet under the circumstances...

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:45.010
You scumbag !

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.000
You're delusional !

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.740
If you continue to
misinterpret my goodwill...

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:53.000
...and try to bring me down to your
inferior standard of ethics...

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.470
...I will teach you proper
etiquette with my own strength !

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.170
You say you'll "teach
me with your strength" ?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.830
One-on-one, you mean ?

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:02.110
Of course.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:07.020
Oh, I feel
so very offended...

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:12.270
...that this ivory-figure-like, thin-armed
boy will fight me one-on-one...

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.420
I must remind you,
Rear Admiral Musel...

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:19.130
...your red-haired subordinate who always
helps you in a pinch is not here with you.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:21.740
If you think you can beat
me with your own strength...

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:24.360
...I suppose you know neither
yourself nor your opponent.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:26.470
Step outside.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:28.240
Sure, we'll step outside.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.880
For you to be beaten up
in front of everyone...

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:35.710
...it would be an unbearable pain
for someone as conceited as you are.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:53.370
You two, I'd like you
to stop right there.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:59.340
A fistfight in a place like this would be
troublesome to the host of this party.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.500
Are you a Military Policeman ?

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.270
I'd like to hear
your name and rank.

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:05.460
No.

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:08.360
I'm Captain Ulrich Kesler.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:13.350
I've been ordered by Admiral Grimmelshausen
to keep watch over this party.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.810
So you're Mr. Kesler.

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:16.670
Huh ?

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.320
When I was sent to serve as in the Military Police sometime ago...

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:23.560
...I heard of you and was
hoping to meet you sometime.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:27.720
I'm flattered, Lord Musel.

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:37.540
In any case, great commanders like the two of you, who are responsible for the future of the Imperial forces...

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:41.770
...would never think of having a fistfight
like low-ranking officers or soldiers would.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:44.020
Therefore, I assume you were both drunk
and wanted to get some air outside.

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:49.320
You two are drunk !

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.020
We'll take you each to
your respective homes.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:58.880
Yes, you're right, Captain.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:01.270
It seems I've sipped a few
too many glasses of wine.

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:07.060
I'll go home with my wife, so I'd appreciate
it if you'd call a car to the front door.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.150
We should thank alcohol.

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:20.890
Because alcohol takes the
blame, humans can be saved.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:35.020
But this isn't the end
of all this, is it ?

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:42.610
Captain Kesler took care
of the situation very well.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:46.240
There's nothing to worry
about, Count Hartenburg.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:51.020
I'm sorry to have caused
you such trouble.

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:04.020
Even though it's almost summer, my
hands and feet feel cold these days.

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.220
By the way...

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:16.850
...I've recently heard a rumor that your
brother-in-law is of the Kaiser's bloodline.

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:21.660
Count, what do you think of it ?

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.220
It's outrageous.

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:30.220
Besides, even if Luneberg is indeed
in the bloodline of the Kaiser...

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:34.450
...unless he's acknowledged officially, it doesn't mean anything.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.670
History is the same way.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:41.720
Unless it's officially acknowledged,
it's merely speculation or legend.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:48.040
Especially in this case, there's no
evidence to suggest such a possibility.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:52.080
We should punish the source
of this rumor for lese majesty.

00:16:52.640 --> 00:17:02.080
From what I've heard, none of the
Kaisers have been a saint in that area.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:05.350
Except for Lord Maximillian Joseph...

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:08.260
...there are very few for
whom we don't have to worry...

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:12.100
...about the possibilities
of illegitimate children.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:18.260
At the risk of being intrusive, what
does your sister think about all this ?

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:25.150
Elizabeth - to tell the truth, I have no idea what she's thinking.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:28.950
I don't even know
if she loves Luneberg.

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:37.220
So, you think Luneberg
is a dangerous person ?

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:43.250
Anyone who has ambitions
and talents is dangerous.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:48.520
It seems this old man is getting all
the answers he wants from me.

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:54.480
I'm a paragon of incompetence,
as everyone including myself knows.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:03.820
But because of it, I've been
in on many people's secrets.

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:07.290
Because I have no ambition
or talent, and I don't gossip...

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:11.320
...people feel safe with me and tell me
things they wouldn't say to other people.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.850
By the way, it seems
I've stayed here too long.

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:20.240
I think I shall bid
you farewell now.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.920
Captain Kesler.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:45.990
Thank you for your work, and there's
one more thing I'd like to ask of you...

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:51.690
As I said, if that
Kesler guy hadn't intruded...

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.860
...I would've beaten up that bastard Luneberg
and picked apart his unstopping {energizer-bunny}tongue.

00:18:55.350 --> 00:19:01.080
That bastard, he dared to call
me a "thin-armed ivory figurine" !

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:05.810
Aside from "thin arms," "ivory
figurine" is more like a compliment.

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:09.080
I mean, he didn't
say "mud doll."

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:15.270
That wouldn't quell his anger - Kircheis
knew this, so he didn't bother to say it.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:22.220
Instead, he decided to report the rest
of his findings on Luneberg to Reinhard.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:33.340
The late fiancé of Mrs. Luneberg we
talked about, Carl Mathius von Folgen...

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:35.650
...he was the fourth
son of Count Folgen.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:41.020
As the fourth son, there was no possibility
he would succeed to the family title...

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:44.270
...so he became a military bureaucrat
with the help of his father.

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:49.230
That was after spending nearly seven years
to graduate from an aristocrat-only school.

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:52.470
He was strictly
confined to deskwork...

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:56.120
...but at one party, he happened
to meet Elizabeth Hartenburg...

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:58.860
...and captured
her heart quickly.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:05.230
Despite protests from their families,
they became engaged.

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:11.210
At that time, Carl Mathius was suddenly
assigned to a front-line base as a Captain.

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:17.490
The base was attacked by the rebel forces,
a.k.a. The Free Planets Alliance army...

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:20.470
...Carl Mathius was killed...

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:23.600
...in the middle of close combat against the famous Rosenritter Regiment.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.770
That was three and
a half years or so ago.

00:20:29.780 --> 00:20:34.410
And the one who actually
killed that man was Luneberg...

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:37.420
Such rumors certainly exist.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:41.260
What do you think,
Lord Reinhard ?

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:45.190
The story is a
little too well-made.

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:48.770
There are so many people
who like such karmic stories.

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:50.560
I can't trust it completely.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:55.690
Then why do you think
Luneberg defected back ?

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.570
Let's see.

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:00.220
When you're confident
in your ability...

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:03.430
...and think you're not getting treated
appropriately for your caliber...

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:08.670
...it's not unusual to want to break out
and escape from such a predicament...

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:10.360
...if provided with a way out.

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:18.270
In my case, too, I was only 10 when my sister was taken away, so there was nothing I could do then.

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:24.120
But if it had happened five years later I might have defected to the Free Planets Alliance with my sister.

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:30.120
Luneberg's present predicament...

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:33.250
...may be one of only many, but real,
possibilities in Reinhard's future...

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:36.580
...and that realization
displeased Reinhard even more.

00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:44.670
On June 14th, the Minister of Home Affairs,
Lord Lichtenlade came to Neue Sansouci...

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:46.670
...to report on
administrative progress.

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:50.730
Once the report on political
matters was finished...

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:55.040
...the topic moved to the subject of the
title for the Kaiser's concubine's brother.

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:59.120
There were many candidates...

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:02.460
...but I've decided to have him succeed
to the title of Count Lohengramm.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:07.330
It's a family famous for military
achievements, and it should suit him well.

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:10.500
But we shouldn't go
forward immediately.

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:13.490
After all, he's
only 18 years old.

00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:17.370
It'll probably be another two years
before the right time comes.

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:18.880
I understand.

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:21.290
There is also some discontent
among the aristocracy...

00:22:21.290 --> 00:22:26.980
...so if you could please be considerate
of that, it would help the situation.

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:28.080
Yes.

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:33.180
By the way, will there be another
campaign before the end of the year ?

00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:39.370
The Ministry of the Military has sent their
campaign plans, haven't you received them ?

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:40.470
Huh ?

00:22:41.470 --> 00:22:42.470
Yes...

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:51.430
Did you hear, Kircheis ?

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:56.030
Starting August 8th, there'll be another
campaign to the Iserlohn area.

00:22:56.030 --> 00:22:58.060
Of course, you and
I will be a part of it.

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:02.190
Will Admiral Grimmelshausen
participate in the campaign, too ?

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:05.260
No, he's pretty much retired.

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:09.130
He can take a nap in his office
in the Ministry of Military Affairs...

00:23:09.130 --> 00:23:12.930
...and leave the battlefield
accomplishments to us.{He can leave it to us for
the battlefield accomplishment.}

00:23:13.310 --> 00:23:18.350
If you take war and ambition out of Lord
Reinhard, there'll be nothing left of him...

00:23:19.670 --> 00:23:21.860
Of course, I guess that
goes for me, too...

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:28.620
Kircheis has never felt bitter
about his present predicament.

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:31.570
That is because Reinhard
has always been with him.

00:23:31.570 --> 00:23:33.570
Because of Reinhard...

00:23:33.570 --> 00:23:37.670
...his troubles don't seem too painful
for him - that was how Kircheis felt...

00:23:37.670 --> 00:23:41.500
...but he might have been taking the
order of things in the wrong way.

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:47.830
It's likely most of his troubles wouldn't
have existed had it not been for Reinhard.

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:50.200
The campaign plan was finalized.

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:51.810
It'll start on August 8th.

00:23:52.050 --> 00:23:53.470
Congratulations.

00:23:53.470 --> 00:23:54.980
"Congratulations," eh ?

00:23:54.980 --> 00:23:56.290
I was talking about you.

00:23:56.290 --> 00:24:00.440
If you go to battle, you'll
surely make a name for yourself.

00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:03.530
So I said "congratulations"...

00:24:07.810 --> 00:24:10.470
Elizabeth, your fiancé was...

00:24:12.140 --> 00:24:13.920
Your fiancé was...

00:24:20.740 --> 00:24:22.370
No, never mind.

00:24:22.370 --> 00:24:24.660
You don't need to know.

00:24:31.010 --> 00:24:36.800
On the next day, the Imperial Fleet's campaign
plan for the Iserlohn area was made public.

00:24:36.800 --> 00:24:43.200
That occurred on June 15th,
Space Year 794, Empire Year 485.

